Extend the Wi-Fi variants' local trusted-LAN root page with a
small settings form for the seven values already accepted by
GET/POST /api/settings from patch 0011. Applied only to
nanoc6-wifi and atoms3-lite-wifi via variants.json;
nanoc6-thread never applies, compiles, links, or serves any of
this.

Scope:
  * MODIFY main/aliro_local_web.cpp: extend kIndexHtml with a
    <form id="settings-form"> that carries seven inputs — one
    number input per timing value with the existing 0..3600
    (auto_relock_seconds) and 0..10000 (*_ms) limits, and one
    color input per RGB field (success/failure/other). A new
    #settings-status element carries the loading / success /
    HTTP-error / invalid-response / network-error text. A new
    <script> block, separate from the existing QR IIFE so a
    settings bug cannot break QR rendering, fetches
    /api/settings on load and populates the form via
    input.value only. populate rejects malformed numeric values
    (auto_relock_seconds must be an integer in 0..3600; each
    *_ms must be an integer in 0..10000; each *_rgb must be
    exactly six hex chars) before reporting loaded or saved.
    On submit, native form.reportValidity() runs first, then
    each of the seven inputs is re-validated in JS; any missing
    or out-of-range value surfaces a clear error and returns
    without a POST, so every POST body contains all seven
    valid values. The POST is application/x-www-form-urlencoded
    (URLSearchParams), RGB stripped of the leading '#'. Every
    status message uses textContent; no dynamic innerHTML is
    introduced. /api/settings is added to the machine-endpoint
    list. Existing QR rendering and error paths are unchanged.

Explicit non-goals for this patch: no settings backend change,
no second store, no cJSON, no external asset or network
request, no logs, no OTA, no reset or reboot, no partition
change.

